  "goodToKnow": "Das Jugendamt is the local youth welfare office, responsible for child protection, support for families, foster care and help in custody (Sorgerecht) and child maintenance matters. It can take children into protective care (in Obhut nehmen) if they're at risk. Parents can also ask it for advice. Every city and district has one, and most Germans first meet it about Kita places or Unterhaltsvorschuss. Plural: die Jugendämter."
